# Build My Personal Life-Awareness AI — Android App + Chrome Extension

I want you to build a connected product consisting of TWO applications:

1. An Android application for my Vivo V2120 (Android 12).
2. A Google Chrome extension for my laptop.

These two applications must communicate with each other through Supabase.

This is not an ordinary productivity app. The central idea is to create an AI that continuously observes my daily activities, understands what I am doing, remembers my life, tracks my goals, and actively communicates with me to help me achieve them.

I will explain the complete vision and expected behaviour. You are responsible for choosing appropriate technologies and implementing the system.

## PART 1 — ANDROID APPLICATION

### 1\. Automatic camera capture

The Android app should automatically capture an image every 15 minutes.

The phone has two cameras:

- Back camera.
- Front camera.

The camera system should be intelligent.

Initially, use the back camera to capture my surroundings. The image should be saved with its exact capture timestamp.

If the back-camera image is black, obstructed, or otherwise unusable, send it for AI interpretation.

If AI determines that the image is unusable, immediately request another image using the front camera instead of waiting for the next 15-minute interval.

If the front camera also produces an unusable image, the AI should contact me through a phone call.

Example:

"Yooo Umer, I can't see anything. What are you doing? Are you hiding from me? 😂"

Other possible situations:

- Back camera captures food: AI identifies what I'm eating.
- Back camera captures my room: AI recognizes the environment.
- Front camera captures me: AI observes my visible activity.
- Front camera captures the ceiling: AI understands that the phone might be lying on a surface.

Never assume something with certainty when the image doesn't establish it.

### 2\. Manual image capture

I also want a button to capture an image whenever I want.

For example, I might want to show the AI my food, my surroundings, something I'm working on, or something I want its opinion about.

Manual images should enter exactly the same processing pipeline as automatic images.

### 3\. Background operation

The app should attempt to operate reliably in the background and continue scheduled captures.

My target device is Vivo V2120 running Android 12.

Investigate Android background camera restrictions and available approaches. Shizuku may be explored as an additional permission/system-access helper if necessary.




### 4\. Supabase connection

Every captured image must be associated with:

- Unique image ID.
- Capture timestamp.
- Camera used.
- Processing status.
- AI interpretation.
- Any relevant error information.

Images must be uploaded to Supabase and made available to the Chrome extension.

The original capture timestamp must always be preserved, even if Gemini processes the image hours later.

## PART 2 — CHROME EXTENSION

The Chrome extension is the visual AI processing engine.

My laptop's Chrome browser stays open throughout the day. You can assume it is available during normal operation.

### 1\. Receive images

The extension should connect to Supabase and continuously check for pending images.

Whenever an image arrives, the extension should receive it and add it to a processing queue.

Each image must be processed only once.

If multiple images accumulate, process them chronologically.

Never lose an image simply because processing failed.

### 2\. Use Gemini through its website

Here is an important part of my approach.

I want to use Gemini's free web interface instead of paying for image-analysis API calls.

The extension should automatically open and interact with Gemini in Chrome.

Create a dedicated Gemini conversation with initial instructions explaining:

- Who I am.
- What my room looks like.
- What I look like.
- Which people are my family and friends.
- What environments I commonly visit.
- How images should be interpreted.
- How uncertain observations should be reported.

I will provide reference images of myself, my family, friends and rooms.

The Gemini conversation should interpret each uploaded image according to these instructions.

For example:

Image interpretation:
"Umer is sitting at a table eating a samosa. Two other people are visible."

Another:
"Umer appears to be exercising at home."

Another:
"The image is almost entirely black. Nothing identifiable is visible."

The extension must also send the original capture timestamp alongside each image.

### 3\. Send interpretations to Android

After Gemini responds, the extension should extract its textual interpretation and send it to Supabase.

The Android app should receive the interpretation and associate it with the original image and timestamp.

### 4\. Free text AI for decision-making

I want to use a free Gemini text model through its web interface for the app's decision-making and conversation intelligence too.

The visual AI describes what it sees.

The text AI evaluates that description against my goals, previous observations, conversations and history.

It decides whether an intervention is necessary.

For example:

Observation:
"Umer is eating a burger at 8:57 PM."

Goal:
"Umer wants to lose weight."

Previous context:
"Umer ate a burger yesterday and exercised today at 5:08 PM."

The AI should understand all of this before deciding what to say.

## PART 3 — THE AI PHONE CALL SYSTEM

This is one of the most important features.

The Android application should be capable of initiating calls to me when the AI decides an intervention is necessary.

Example:

At 8:57 PM, Gemini identifies me eating a burger.

The text AI evaluates the observation and decides to intervene.

The Android app receives the prepared message and calls me.

When I answer, it speaks using text-to-speech.

Example:

"Umer, why the fuck are you eating this? Did you forget your goal?"

I respond:

"I'm hungry. I haven't eaten properly today."

The app records my response, converts my speech to text, and sends it to the Chrome extension through Supabase.

The extension submits my response to the same Gemini conversation.

Gemini considers the conversation history and generates a reply.

The extension extracts that reply and sends it back to the Android app.

The app speaks the reply through text-to-speech.

This creates a continuous conversational loop.

The conversation should continue until either I end it or the AI concludes it naturally.

Every conversation must be recorded and associated with the relevant events.

For the first version, use ordinary available text-to-speech. Voice cloning can be added later.

Important: Implement calls through a supported Android calling mechanism, with the required permissions and user controls. Do not assume arbitrary background calling is automatically permitted.

## PART 4 — MY GOALS AND PERSONAL CONTEXT

I should be able to tell the AI what I want to achieve.

Examples:

- I want to lose weight.
- I want to learn programming.
- I want to earn money.
- I want to stop wasting time.
- I want to study mathematics.
- I want to improve my daily routine.

The AI should understand my goals, help create plans, and continuously compare my actual behaviour against those plans.

For example, if my goal is weight loss, it should understand:

- What I eat.
- When I eat.
- Whether I exercise.
- How often I exercise.
- My previous food observations.
- My previous conversations about food.

If my goal is studying, it should understand my study activity and compare it with my intended study schedule.

The system must support multiple goals simultaneously.

## PART 5 — LONG-TERM MEMORY AND LIFE TIMELINE

I want a persistent record of my life.

The system should maintain:

1. Image history.
2. AI-generated descriptions.
3. Capture timestamps.
4. Daily activity timelines.
5. Goals and plans.
6. Conversations with the AI.
7. Important decisions.
8. Behavioural patterns.
9. Historical progress.

Use a RAG-based memory system so the text AI can retrieve relevant previous information instead of receiving my entire history in every request.

For example, I should be able to ask:

"What did I eat yesterday?"

"How many times did I exercise this week?"

"When was the last time I studied mathematics?"

"Compare my productivity this month with last month."

The AI should use actual recorded information rather than inventing answers.

## PART 6 — THE PERSONALITY

I don't want a generic corporate assistant.

I want an AI companion that talks naturally, remembers previous conversations, understands context, and can use humour, sarcasm, strictness and casual language.

It should be able to challenge me when my actions conflict with my goals.

However, it should also understand explanations.

If I eat a burger because I'm with friends, it shouldn't blindly accuse me of failure.

Its personality should feel like a continuing relationship rather than isolated notifications.

## PART 7 — THE FIRST BUILD

Do not attempt to implement every advanced feature simultaneously.

Build the foundation first, but structure the project so that future features can be added without rebuilding everything.

My priorities:

1. Working Android application.
2. Automatic and manual image capture.
3. Timestamped image storage.
4. Supabase connection.
5. Working Chrome extension.
6. Automatic Gemini image processing.
7. Return image interpretations to Android.
8. Basic text AI decision-making.
9. Text-to-speech and conversational interaction.
10. Long-term memory and RAG.

Create a clean, understandable interface.

The Android app and Chrome extension must function as one connected product, not two unrelated prototypes.

